  "autoEscalation": "field_manager: any computed impact >= S1 on an APPLYING mutation routes through ChangeRequest. admin: always allow including S3 (מנהל-על שליטה מלאה) — R1 resolved: no role above admin, so admin S3 cannot deadlock. EXEMPTION: domino.compute is a dry-run preview — it never mutates and NEVER creates a ChangeRequest, whatever impact class it computes; it stays allow + scope-checked (field_manager: own sites only). focus_worker never receives the full graph (data minimization).",
  "changeRequestRules": {
    "stateMachine": "proposed -> pending_review -> approved(applied) | rejected",
    "editPolicy": "A pending ChangeRequest cannot be edited. Proposer withdraws and resubmits (new id). Locked decision, per QA charter AC-RBAC-5 option.",
    "selfApproval": "Forbidden for cross-scope changes; admin-only approve.",
    "staleBase": "Approve on a moved base graph version => 409 stale, re-propose. Never force-apply."
  },
  "denyByDefault": "Any action x role combination not listed is denied (403), including unknown actions.",
  "reportApplyRule": {
    "rule": "report.status.create auto-applies the reporter's OWN task delay when computed impact is S0 and the task is unlocked. Anything above S0, or a locked task, becomes ChangeRequest pending_review.",
    "never": "A report is never a back-door task.move on another user's task or above S0 impact. (QA C2)"
  },
  "migrationNote": "v1.2 -> v1.3 (2026-09-14): additive row 'report.resolve' (POST /v1/reports/:id/resolve). Pure handled-state on StatusReport: no graph effect, no effect on spawned CRs. admin=allow; field_manager=scope (own sites); focus_worker=deny. No existing cell changed. v1.3 -> v1.4 (2026-09-15): additive rows whitelist.invite/list/approve/reject (contracts v1.18 §15). admin=allow; field_manager/focus_worker=deny. No existing cell changed."
